    "evidence": "The screen strongly replaces generic accuracy with deployment-relevant fraud metrics: PR-AUC, constrained-FPR recall, calibration, alert load, latency, confusion counts, value caught/blocked, and Semantic/Provenance ablations. However, it does not visibly connect these results to intent-integrity attacks, Mastercard-specific payment flows, challenge data, or an end-to-end defended transaction. The displayed numbers also lack visible dataset, sample-size, baseline, and threshold-selection provenance, so the hackathon claim is not fully demonstrated.",
